## 1. Problem we solve

Developers ship web apps and don’t know OWASP. They can’t hire InfoSec for every sprint.  
They need: open app in **Vigil Browser** → run **safe authorized checks** → see “what broke / what’s risky” → get **fix** applied in the project → retest.

Commercial: companies buy “اختبروا الموقع ده هل يتاخد؟ وقولولنا نصلّح إزاي” as a **service/product**, not as hacking-as-a-service against third parties.

---

> **عربي:** قواعد إلزامية

## 2. Guardrails (non-negotiable)

- [ ] Target must be one of: `localhost` / `127.0.0.1` / project preview URL / user-configured **allowlisted** hosts  
- [ ] For non-local hosts: require **ownership confirmation** (DNS TXT, file upload, admin checkbox + typed CONFIRM, or org-verified domain in Firestore)  
- [ ] Block tools if URL is not allowlisted — hard fail in sidecar policy (not only prompt)  
- [ ] No credential stuffing against third-party sites; no malware distribution; no ransomware  
- [ ] Prefer **known scanners’ safe modes** + **passive** checks first; active checks = explicit user Start  
- [ ] Rate limits; no DoS stress modes in v1 (or separate “load” product later with warnings)  
- [ ] Findings stored as **security reports** in account (Firestore) — **not** full exploit kits shared publicly  
- [ ] Agent default: **remediate** (patch, headers, validation) — not “how to weaponize”  
- [ ] Legal/ToS: “only systems you own or are authorized to test”  

