## 5. Capability map (dreams + phases)

> **عربي:** تعليم للمبتدئ أمنيًا

### 5.1 Education layer (for security-illiterate users) — CRITICAL

- [ ] Plain Arabic explanations: what XSS/SQLi/CSRF/IDOR/… means in one short paragraph  
- [ ] “Why it matters” + “how attackers abuse” at **high level** (no step-by-step crime manual)  
- [ ] Fix guidance tied to **their stack** (detect Express/Next/Laravel/Django/ASP.NET from repo)  

> **عربي:** فحص سلبي/إعدادات

### 5.2 Passive / config review (safe, repo-based)

- [ ] Dependency CVE scan (`npm audit`, `pip-audit`, OSV) — already adjacent to agent tools  
- [ ] Secret leak scan in workspace (API keys in client bundles)  
- [ ] Security headers checklist on responses (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, …) via Browser  
- [ ] Cookie flags (Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite)  
- [ ] HTTPS / mixed content  
- [ ] CORS misconfiguration heuristics on **own** API  
- [ ] Auth cookie/session basics in preview  

> **عربي:** فحص نشط مصرّح

### 5.3 Active checks on authorized target (Vigil Browser + optional scanners)

High-level categories (OWASP-aligned) — implement via **safe probes** / integrated tools, not ad-hoc malware:

- [ ] **Injection** (SQL/NoSQL/command) — parameterized probes on forms/APIs user maps; stop on confirm  
- [ ] **XSS** reflected/stored — input reflection checks  
- [ ] **Authn/Authz** — unauthenticated access to `/admin`, IDOR-style same-role object access **on fixtures**  
- [ ] **CSRF** — missing token heuristics on state-changing forms  
- [ ] **Path / file** — obvious traversal on upload/download endpoints if present  
- [ ] **Security misconfig** — directory listing, default pages, verbose errors  
- [ ] **Sensitive data** — stack traces, `.env` exposed, source maps in prod preview  

**Integrations (prefer battle-tested engines over inventing exploits):**
- [ ] Optional **OWASP ZAP** baseline/api (local process)  
- [ ] Optional **Nuclei** with **safe/informative** templates only (curated allowlist of templates)  
- [ ] Playwright/`browser_*` for click-path + screenshot evidence  

> **عربي:** إصلاح وإعادة اختبار

### 5.4 Fix & verify

- [ ] Finding → suggested patch (code + config + headers middleware)  
- [ ] Plan Mode: security remediation plan  
- [ ] Retest button per finding  
- [ ] “Secure baseline” badge when pack passes on preview  

> **عربي:** تقرير للبيع

### 5.5 Commercial Secure Report (sellable)

- [ ] Package entitlement `feature.vigilSecure` / SKU **Vigil Secure**  
- [ ] Run pack → **Report** (AR/EN): executive summary + technical findings + fix checklist  
- [ ] Export PDF / Markdown; push Bugs to **Azure DevOps**  
- [ ] Customer portal on Vigil Web: past reports, schedule monthly retest (`Schedule`)  
- [ ] Clear disclaimer: not a certified pentest unless partner process added later  

